 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Mostly the bride's side pays for the wedding, usually with help from the bride and groom's parents. You could ask his parents if the original offer stands, or go with a per couple donation. Either is pretty usual. Not at all. And it gives you some money for rainy day in case some adults can't make it. Then it' their wedding, and you' find out who's sitting alone at the back. It's worth asking politely and being prepared to make the call. That's the right call. Thanks!",
